From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 7778777 <7778777@7778777.online>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:19:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mach-defpager: supply a copy of the truncated last page

When a memory object is truncated to a size that is not a multiple of
the page size, the default pager asks the kernel to return the last
page, clears its end and supplies it again.  It sent the returned page
itself, with the deallocate bit.  GNU Mach wires a page that it hands to
the default pager (vm_pageout_setup), on top of the wiring of the
pager's address space, and expects the pager to free it; stealing it
back fails

  vm_map_copyin_page_list: Assertion `m->wire_count == 1' failed.

and the kernel stops.  ftruncate of a tmpfs file triggers it once the
last page is resident and dirty, for example a mapped file that is
shrunk to 10 bytes.

* mach-defpager/default_pager.c (seqnos_memory_object_data_return):
Supply the page without the deallocate bit, then deallocate it.
---
 mach-defpager/default_pager.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mach-defpager/default_pager.c b/mach-defpager/default_pager.c
index 813a0a53..3d0e1254 100644
--- a/mach-defpager/default_pager.c
+++ b/mach-defpager/default_pager.c
@@ -2695,13 +2695,21 @@ seqnos_memory_object_data_return(default_pager_t	ds,
 	    vm_size_t tail_size = round_page(limit) - limit;
 	    memset((void *) tail, 0, tail_size);
 
+	    /* Supply a copy and free ADDR below, like every returned page.
+	       The kernel wired this page for the pageout, on top of the
+	       wiring of our whole address space, and expects us to free
+	       it: sent on with the deallocate bit, it fails GNU Mach's
+	       vm_map_copyin_page_list: Assertion `m->wire_count == 1'.  */
 	    memory_object_data_supply(pager_request, trunc_page(limit), addr,
-				      vm_page_size, TRUE, VM_PROT_NONE,
+				      vm_page_size, FALSE, VM_PROT_NONE,
 				      TRUE, MACH_PORT_NULL);
 	    dstruct_lock(ds);
 	    ds->dpager.byte_limit = round_page(limit);
 	    dstruct_unlock(ds);
 	    pager_port_finish_write(ds);
+	    if (vm_deallocate(default_pager_self, addr, data_cnt)
+		!= KERN_SUCCESS)
+		panic(here,my_name);
 
 	    return(KERN_SUCCESS);
 	  }
